Sequence shape, which decides whether the facade's byte[] reader costs
anything here: gRPC delivered 5508 SEGMENTED bodies and 0 single-segment,
copying 2,976,644,376 bytes in total to flatten them. The copy is charged to the
facade arms; a ReadOnlySequence reader is what would remove it.

